  "notes": "All 3 backends updated with adaptive timeout wiring:\n\n1. DockerSpawnBackend: worker.sh template now uses `TIMEOUT=${TASK_TIMEOUT:-<default>}` instead of hardcoded `timeout 1200`. TASK_TIMEOUT env var is passed via docker run -e. effectiveTimeout computed from opts.taskTimeoutSeconds ?? this.timeoutSeconds.\n\n2. tmux.ts: WORKER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS marked @deprecated. spawnWorker() now accepts `taskTimeoutSeconds` in opts and passes it to buildWorkerCommand() as the timeoutSeconds parameter.\n\n3. spawn-backend.ts: SpawnBackendOptions gains `taskTimeoutSeconds?: number` field. TmuxBackend.spawn() passes it through. SubprocessBackend.spawn() creates a fresh SubprocessSpawnBackend with taskTimeoutSeconds*1000 as defaultTimeoutMs when override is provided.\n\n4. DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (docker) and WORKER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (tmux) both marked @deprecated but kept for backward compat.\n\ntsc --noEmit: 0 errors in my files (existing errors from Task 1/2 dependency not yet merged: TimeoutConfig, DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_CONFIG, ResolvedConfig.timeout — these are pre-existing).\n\nTests: 18/18 PASS in tests/orchestra/spawn-timeout.test.ts. Docker test failures (6 in tests/docker/docker-hb.test.ts) are pre-existing atomicWriteHb assertions unrelated to this task.",
